---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CodeTabs from '../components/CodeTabs.astro';
const origin = 'https://axond.dev';
---
<Layout title="Quickstart — Axond" description="Install Axond, connect OpenAI, and make your first routed request.">
<div class="site-shell">
      <header class="site-header">
        <a class="wordmark" href="/">
          axond
        </a>
        <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
          <a href="/#get-started">Install</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/Litvue/axond">GitHub ↗</a>
        </nav>
      </header>
      <main class="quickstart" id="main">
        <p class="eyebrow">LOCAL QUICKSTART</p>
        <h1>Your first routed request.</h1>
        <p>
          After 
          <a class="text-link" href="/#get-started">
            installing Axond
          </a>
          , connect an OpenAI API key and start a local gateway.
        </p>
        <section class="quickstart-step">
          <h2>1. Configure and run</h2>
          <p>
            Run these commands in a new directory. Replace 
            <code>your-provider-key</code> with your OpenAI API key. Keep this
            terminal open.
          </p>
          <CodeTabs
            name="run"
            entries={{
              "macOS/Linux": `mkdir -p axond-local\ncd axond-local\ncurl -fsSLo axond.toml ${origin}/axond.toml\nexport PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:$PATH"\nexport OPENAI_API_KEY="your-provider-key"\nexport GW_INBOUND_PLATFORM_KEY="quickstart-platform-key"\naxond`,
              Windows: `New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path axond-local\nSet-Location axond-local\nInvoke-WebRequest ${origin}/axond.toml -OutFile axond.toml\n$env:Path += ";$env:LOCALAPPDATA\\Programs\\axond"\n$env:OPENAI_API_KEY = "your-provider-key"\n$env:GW_INBOUND_PLATFORM_KEY = "quickstart-platform-key"\naxond`,
            }}
          />
          <p class="quickstart-note">
            The <a href="/axond.toml">example configuration</a> listens only on
            your machine and stores usage in a local SQLite file. The gateway
            key shown here is for local testing.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section class="quickstart-step">
          <h2>2. Set a budget</h2>
          <p>
            In a second terminal, set a $10 budget for the platform namespace.
            Axond requires a budget before forwarding requests.
          </p>
          <CodeTabs
            name="budget"
            entries={{
              "macOS/Linux": `curl -fsS -X PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/namespaces/platform/budgets/quickstart \\\n  -H "Authorization: Bearer quickstart-platform-key" \\\n  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\\n  -d '{"limit_microdollars":10000000}'`,
              Windows: `Invoke-RestMethod -Method Put \`\n  -Uri http://localhost:8080/api/v1/namespaces/platform/budgets/quickstart \`\n  -Headers @{Authorization="Bearer quickstart-platform-key"} \`\n  -ContentType application/json \`\n  -Body '{"limit_microdollars":10000000}'`,
            }}
          />
        </section>
        <section class="quickstart-step">
          <h2>3. Make a request</h2>
          <p>
            Use your gateway key and namespace URL with your usual OpenAI
            client. This request uses your provider account and incurs provider
            charges.
          </p>
          <CodeTabs
            name="request"
            entries={{
              "macOS/Linux": `curl -fsS http://localhost:8080/ns/platform/v1/chat/completions \\\n  -H "Authorization: Bearer quickstart-platform-key" \\\n  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \\\n  -d '{"model":"openai/gpt-4o","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Hello, Axond."}],"max_tokens":64}'`,
              Windows: `Invoke-RestMethod -Method Post \`\n  -Uri http://localhost:8080/ns/platform/v1/chat/completions \`\n  -Headers @{Authorization="Bearer quickstart-platform-key"} \`\n  -ContentType application/json \`\n  -Body '{"model":"openai/gpt-4o","messages":[{"role":"user","content":"Hello, Axond."}],"max_tokens":64}'`,
            }}
          />
          <p>
            <a class="text-link" href="/#examples">
              Python and TypeScript examples →
            </a>
          </p>
        </section>
        <p>
          For more providers and deployment settings, see the 
          <a
            class="text-link"
            href="https://github.com/Litvue/axond/blob/main/docs/configuration.md"
          >
            configuration guide ↗
          </a>
          .
        </p>
      </main>
      <footer>
        <p>
          MIT licensed. Made by the team behind 
          <a href="https://litvue.com">Litvue</a>.
        </p>
      </footer>
    </div>
</Layout>
